3d:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"consider_expired_after_s"}]," is the one people are surprised by. When set, an\nobject whose ",["$","code",null,{"children":"last_modified"}]," is older than this many seconds is reported as\n",["$","em",null,{"children":"not existing"}],", even though it is still in the bucket. Pair it with a bucket\nlifecycle rule whose window is longer by a comfortable margin (a few days):\nthe rule deletes the object, and this setting stops Forge handing out a\ndigest that is about to disappear. Clients that get a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"NotFound"}],"\nre-upload."]}]
