43:["$","$L74",null,{"children":[["$","$L75",null,{"title":"Every request fails with a credentials error","id":"every-request-fails-with-a-credentials-error","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["For ",["$","code",null,{"children":"aws"}],", the credential chain found nothing. Confirm the process can see\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID"}]," and ",["$","code",null,{"children":"AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY"}],", or that the instance/task\nrole is attached and reachable. For ",["$","code",null,{"children":"r2"}],", set ",["$","code",null,{"children":"access_key_id"}]," and\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"secret_access_key"}]," explicitly, because R2 tokens are not in the AWS chain."]}]}],["$","$L75",null,{"title":"TLS verification fails against an on-premises endpoint","id":"tls-verification-fails-against-an-on-premises-endpoint","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Set ",["$","code",null,{"children":"root_certificates"}]," to the PEM bundle for the CA that signed the\nendpoint's certificate. Do not reach for ",["$","code",null,{"children":"insecure_allow_http"}],", which\ndisables transport security entirely and is meant only for a local test\ndouble."]}]}],["$","$L75",null,{"title":"Builds are slow even though the cache is hitting","id":"builds-are-slow-even-though-the-cache-is-hitting","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["You're going to the bucket on every read. Check that the store is the ",["$","code",null,{"children":"slow"}],"\nhalf of a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"fast_slow"}]," pair and that the ",["$","code",null,{"children":"fast"}]," half's ",["$","code",null,{"children":"eviction_policy"}]," isn't\nso small it evicts everything before it's re-read."]}]}],["$","$L75",null,{"title":"The bucket bill is dominated by requests, not storage","id":"the-bucket-bill-is-dominated-by-requests-not-storage","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Same cause. A build cache issues enormous numbers of small existence checks\nand reads; object storage prices those individually. A local fast tier, and\nan ",["$","$L1b",null,{"href":"/how-to/stores/compose-stores","children":["$","code",null,{"children":"existence_cache"}]}]," in front of the slow\nstore, are the two levers."]}]}],["$","$L75",null,{"title":"Large uploads fail but small ones succeed","id":"large-uploads-fail-but-small-ones-succeed","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Objects of 5 MB and above go through multipart upload, so check that the\ncredential can ",["$","code",null,{"children":"CreateMultipartUpload"}],", ",["$","code",null,{"children":"UploadPart"}],", ",["$","code",null,{"children":"CompleteMultipartUpload"}],"\nand ",["$","code",null,{"children":"AbortMultipartUpload"}],"; a policy that only allows ",["$","code",null,{"children":"PutObject"}]," breaks\nexactly at that size. Also check ",["$","code",null,{"children":"max_retry_buffer_per_request"}]," if you have\nlowered it: a single-request upload larger than the buffer cannot be replayed\nafter a transient failure, and setting it to zero disables upload buffering\nentirely, which trades retry safety for memory."]}]}],["$","$L75",null,{"title":"Objects exist in the bucket but Forge reports them missing","id":"objects-exist-in-the-bucket-but-forge-reports-them-missing","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Check ",["$","code",null,{"children":"consider_expired_after_s"}],". A non-zero value makes objects older than\nthat window invisible on purpose. If you didn't intend that, set it back\nto ",["$","code",null,{"children":"0"}],"."]}]}]]}]
